# Line endings are content as far as a migration checksum is concerned.
#
# sqlx records a SHA-384 of each migration's bytes when it applies it, and
# refuses to run against a database whose recorded checksum disagrees with the
# file. With `core.autocrlf=true` and no rule here, a Windows checkout produces
# CRLF and a Linux one produces LF, so the *same commit* yields two different
# checksums — and a database migrated on one machine cannot be migrated on the
# other. That is not hypothetical: it happened to 0036 on 2026-09-14.
#
# Pinning LF makes the checksum a property of the commit rather than of whoever
# ran it. Use `cargo run -p storage --example normalize_checksums` to re-record
# a database that was migrated under the old behaviour; it refuses to touch a
# row whose difference is anything but line endings.
migrations/*.sql text eol=lf

# Everything else keeps the platform default, and that is a live trade-off rather
# than a settled one. A repo-wide renormalisation would be a thousand-file
# whitespace diff; against that, `migrations/` is no longer the only place where
# bytes are compared.
#
# The structural invariants read their own source with `include_str!` and split on
# newlines -- `gate.rs`'s `no_construction_of_the_gate_can_disable_trial_enforcement`,
# `lib.rs`'s dispatch-arm scan, `falsification.rs`'s guide lookup. Under
# `core.autocrlf` those see CRLF on a Windows checkout and LF in CI, from the same
# commit. Two of them failed exactly that way on 2026-09-15 and reported it as a
# missing heading and a missing impl block, which is the worst kind of wrong: a
# structural test that says the structure is gone when only the newlines changed.
#
# Each of those now normalises before it reads, which fixes them and does not fix
# the next one. **Any new `include_str!` test must normalise, or this file must
# gain `*.rs text eol=lf` and the renormalisation that comes with it.**

# Binary: never touched.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf   binary
*.parquet binary
